      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While maximizing resources might seem mathematically efficient in a narrow sense, using historically biased data as a primary predictor often leads to a \"chasing the target\" dynamic that ultimately increases overall crime rates and distrust. Algorithms trained heavily on these proxies frequently degrade into feedback loops where over-policing creates more negative outcomes that the system then mistakes for proof of higher risk. A more robust utilitarian approach would pivot from static demographics to predictive, real-time indicators that reflect actual future risk trajectories for every neighborhood.",
